  "style": {
    "id": "weather-map",
    "name": "Weather Map",
    "description": "A broadcast weather map made physical: a raised relief model of an invented landmass (seeded coastline, hills, depth-shaded sea) on a studio table, soft cloud puffs floating above it casting shadows, and bold broadcast graphics on a glass layer above: white isobars from a pressure field, red warm and blue cold fronts with marching symbols, big H and L centres, flowing wind arrows, temperature bands draped on the land and weather icons that pop up over invented places. Fronts and pressure centres advance as functions of time; clouds and their shadows travel with them, and a place's icon and colour band change the moment its front arrives, while the camera sweeps like a broadcast fly-over.",
